-- title:
--   Strict ordinarity at p for Hecke-ring points with non-flat ρ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field, and $p$ a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over the residue field of $\mathcal O$ which factors through a finite level and is absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to the algebraic closure). Let $N\ge 1$ be an integer all of whose prime divisors lie in the finite set $S$ of naturals, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal O$, such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_i\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ be monoid homomorphisms (written multiplicatively), and let $\alpha\colon\{1,\dots,t\}\to$ residue field of $\mathcal O$. Put $L=N\,(\prod_i q_i)\,r$ and let $H_Q=$ `HQ N r qv p πΔ` be the subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ cut out as the intersection of `HR` with the kernel of `piQ`; assume the operators `op` attached to the generators commute pairwise (`OpComm`) and commute with the diamond operators [`CohCarrier.diamondL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55) (`DiaComm`). Let $\mathcal O'$ be a second characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field, an $\mathcal O$-algebra via a local homomorphism, and let $\lambda$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the Hecke ring `HeckeRing N r qv S 𝒪 (HQ …) θ α` (the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O}$ of the module `ML` generated by `heckeRingGens`) to $\mathcal O'$. Let $\rho$ be a Galois representation on a free $\mathcal O'$-module of rank $2$ with adically continuous action, such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $\ell$ as a non-unit and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, one has $\operatorname{tr}\rho(\sigma)=\lambda(T_\ell)$, and such that the residual representation of $\rho$ is isomorphic to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Assume finally $p\mid L$, $p^2\nmid L$, and that $\bar\rho$, viewed as a Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal O$ regarded as a local ring, is not flat at $p$ in the sense of `IsFlatAt`. Then $\rho$ is strictly ordinary at $p$: $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O'$, and for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $p$ as a non-unit there is an $\mathcal O'$-line $L_P=\mathcal O'\cdot b_0$ spanned by the first vector of some basis of $\rho.V$, stable under the decomposition group of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, with $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in L_P$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup and all $v$, and such that each $\sigma$ in the decomposition group acts on $L_P$ by a scalar $x$ and on the quotient by a scalar $z$ with $x-az\in(p^n)$ whenever $\sigma$ acts on the $p^n$-th roots of unity by $\mu\mapsto\mu^a$.
--
--   This is the pointwise form, over a discrete valuation ring, of the assertion that the modular Galois representation attached to the Taylor–Wiles-level Hecke ring is strictly ordinary at $p$ when $p$ divides the level exactly once and the residual representation is not finite flat at $p$; the local behaviour at $p$ comes from the theory of the ordinary/flat dichotomy for eigenforms of weight two. It feeds the corresponding statement for the Hecke ring itself, [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isStrictOrdinaryAt_of_dvd_level_of_not_isFlatAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isStrictOrdinaryAt_of_dvd_level_of_not_isFlatAt), where the strict lines at the various points are glued.
